<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19734" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gnĭdus or Gnĭdos</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cnĭd-</span></b> ), i,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κνίδος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Doric city in
			Caria</i>, <i>celebrated for its statue of Venus</i>,
				<i>the workmanship of Praxiteles;</i> now <i>Cnido</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 16,
				2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 28, 29, § 104</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				30, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 28, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 10,
				531</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. de Imp. Pomp. 12,
			33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 37, 16</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Deriv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gnĭdĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cn-</span></b> ), a um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Gnidus</i>, <i>Gnidian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Venus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					36, 5, 4, § 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gyges,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 2, 5, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">granum,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the seed of the mezereon</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					13, 21, 35, § 114</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arundo,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Gnidian writingreed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 7, 50</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">also called nodi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 74</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gnĭdii</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cn-</span></b> ),
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Gnidus</i>, <i>Gnidians</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 60, § 135</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				36, 5, 4, § 20</span></i>.</div>
